  "historical_output_text": " It is the afternoon when work and family commitments leave time just sufficient but insufficient; an evening that has lost light before one's thoughts do.\nIt starts on what I had imagined as just an unoccupied hour and it quickly grows in length into something closer towards two, perhaps closer still than an exact two but it seems, by that moment's close to stretch past a full quarter after it. It comes when time and attention both run scarce. A weeknight that feels not only long for lacklarks in light; the evening has left me early.\nBut there was work in the still space that has filled my hands to occupy this space in my days.\nThis space holds something of use.\nThis something that holds, holds something, in the quiet hours after my days begin, and just in those moments after which, it will cease again as my time has been.\nWhat it takes",
